# ADR 0001 — Development Workflow

- **Status:** Proposed
- **Date:** <!-- YYYY-MM-DD -->

## Context

{{ project_name }} needs a consistent, traceable delivery process so that
both humans and AI agents build the same way every milestone, with quality
gates and human review.

This ADR is a *starter* generated by the Copier foundation template. Replace
its contents (and update the Status / Date fields) once your project has
settled on its actual workflow.

## Decision

Adopt a delivery pipeline along these lines (customise to your project):

| Layer | Tool | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Delivery workflow | _e.g. CCPM_ | PRD → Epic → Tasks → GitHub Issues, tracking, close/merge/archive |
| Implementation agent | _e.g. Claude Code_ | Executes one bounded issue / task at a time |
| Quality gate | GitHub Actions CI | install, lint, build, tests, security checks |
| Workflow filesystem | Copier | initializes `docs/` and `.github/` templates |
| Final approval | Human review | scope, architecture, tools, PRs, milestones |

Suggested hard rules:

- No product feature without a spec and a tracked task / GitHub Issue.
- One bounded issue at a time; stop for human review.
- Tools are installed via official methods only, recorded in an ADR / setup note.
- CI must pass before merge; human review is the final gate.

## Consequences

- All work is traceable from milestone → spec → task → PR.
- Some process overhead for small changes, accepted in exchange for
  traceability and reviewability.
- Future ADRs supersede this one as the workflow matures.
